00:19:30.090 --> 00:19:32.070
I'd like to win prizes.

00:19:32.070 --> 00:19:34.210
- Welcome everyone to the Fall Festival

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:35.990
and Crop Competition.

00:19:35.990 --> 00:19:38.590
Today we celebrate your fine farming skills

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:42.210
and award blue ribbons the very best fruits and vegetables.

00:19:42.210 --> 00:19:45.690
The first category to be judged is carrots.

00:19:45.690 --> 00:19:53.870
I'm sorry, but the rules clearly state

00:19:53.870 --> 00:19:56.620
that the crops must be presented as they were harvested

00:19:56.620 --> 00:19:58.540
and not cut or prepared in any way.

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:00.000
These carrots are disqualified.

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:02.700
Agreed! Yes, disqualified!

00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:05.700
Yes! Delicious! I mean, disqualified!

00:20:10.070 --> 00:20:13.240
It was on the entry form, I forgot that.

00:20:13.240 --> 00:20:15.860
I'm so sorry, Squeaks.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:19.860
But you should be proud, Squeaks. Just look at the judges!

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:21.860
They're not even tasting those other carrots!

00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:27.280
You know, I am proud. I shouldn't have been ashamed of our carrots.

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:30.000
They did look funny on the outside, but they were so...

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.450
So special and wonderful on the inside.

00:20:32.450 --> 00:20:33.730
And that's what matters.

00:20:33.730 --> 00:20:36.550
I'm starting to think the Bumpy carrots could've won.

00:20:36.550 --> 00:20:38.910
I wish we hadn't made them all into roses.

00:20:38.910 --> 00:20:40.510
Attention, everyone!

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:45.040
It seems like we have a replacement for this carrot.

00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:46.530
What did you do?

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:49.130
I know that Bumpy is good enough to win that blue ribbon.

00:20:49.130 --> 00:20:51.790
He's perfect in his own way, lumps and all.

00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:53.880
Sparkle, Bumpy, sparkle.

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:55.800
This is your time to shine.

00:20:55.800 --> 00:20:57.220
It's my time to shine.

00:20:57.220 --> 00:20:58.400
I'm Bumpy.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:00.000
Hal, are you sure this is

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.500
Okay, I mean they're nibbling him.

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:05.100
So he'll be a little shorter.

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:07.440
Squeaks deserves a chance to win.

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:09.440
You have got to be kidding me.

00:21:09.440 --> 00:21:11.980
That lumpy, ugly carrot is no match

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:14.740
for my perfect, beautiful carrots.

00:21:16.400 --> 00:21:19.280
And the winner of the carrot category is

00:21:19.280 --> 00:21:21.280
Squeaks!

00:21:28.380 --> 00:21:30.000
Ribbon?

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:31.890
so many oceans.

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:34.910
I promised that I wouldn't cry, but here I am.

00:21:34.910 --> 00:21:36.070
- What? What?

00:21:36.070 --> 00:21:38.730
Can you not see the perfection of my crop?

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:40.830
These are gorgeous carrots!

00:21:40.830 --> 00:21:41.650
Gorgeous!

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:43.650
Yes, but you didn't grow them.

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:44.930
You bought them at the store,

00:21:44.930 --> 00:21:46.570
and that's against the rules, Ronald!

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:47.410
- What?

00:21:47.410 --> 00:21:48.250
- Mwah!

00:21:49.340 --> 00:21:52.840
- I worked for months to grow these flawless beauties.

00:21:52.840 --> 00:21:55.740
- Uh, sir, there are labels on them.

00:21:56.920 --> 00:21:59.210
- Looks like you forgot to peel them off.

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:00.000
Anyway.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:03.740
Even if you didn't buy them, Squeaks' Carrot just tasted better.

00:22:03.740 --> 00:22:05.640
A lot better!

00:22:05.640 --> 00:22:08.110
Fine! Fine! Keep your blue ribbons!

00:22:08.110 --> 00:22:11.370
I don't like prizes. I didn't want any prizes.

00:22:13.500 --> 00:22:15.020
I don't think I believe him.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:17.760
Uh, excuse me. Hi. Um, is it too late to enter?

00:22:17.760 --> 00:22:19.660
'Cause these are some mighty-tasted apples.

00:22:19.660 --> 00:22:22.240
But I wasn't gonna enter 'em 'cause they look a little funny.

00:22:22.240 --> 00:22:24.710
Like they have smooshed-up faces, see?

00:22:24.710 --> 00:22:27.260
But I figured that if Squeaks' Carrot could win on taste,

00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:30.000
then, uh, well, my funny little old apples might have a chance

00:22:31.820 --> 00:22:33.720
- And I'd like to enter my peppers.

00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:35.000
They're skinny and stripey,

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:37.060
but they're super crunchy and yummy.

00:22:37.060 --> 00:22:38.720
- Well, there you have it, folks.

00:22:38.720 --> 00:22:39.600
Don't be shy.

00:22:39.600 --> 00:22:41.960
Even if you have less than perfect looking produce

00:22:41.960 --> 00:22:44.860
that you find particularly tasty, please enter.

00:22:44.860 --> 00:22:57.540
Ha!

00:22:57.540 --> 00:22:59.090
- This is your blue ribbon.

00:22:59.090 --> 00:23:00.000
You did all that hard.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:04.980
work, right Bumpy? That's right Hal, I'm Bumpy. I know I worked hard, but our carrots

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:10.150
never would have won at all if you hadn't believed in them. I owe it all to you Hal, thank you.

00:23:10.150 --> 00:23:16.270
To Team Squeaks! Team Squeaks! And I'm Bumpy.

00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:22.560
Nature Cat, Squeaks, Daisy, and Hal are cartoon characters and not real animals. To

00:23:22.560 --> 00:23:26.460
keep all of our animal friends safe, check with a grown-up before you bring a

00:23:26.460 --> 00:23:29.600
pet on your next nature adventure.
